312 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 216 0 R
/T (Software Explanation)
/E (Software Explanation)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
313 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 216 0 R
/T (Section Overview:)
/E (Section Overview:)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
314 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 216 0 R
/E (We chose Betaflight as our flight controller software. Betaflight is a reliable open-source configurator with broad compatibility and is recommended by the manufacturer of our flight controller.  Furthermore, we also used the AM32.ca website \(AM32 configurator\) to update the firmware and adjust the default configuration on our T-Motor ESC. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
315 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 216 0 R
/E (Along with this, we also used the ExpressLRS configurator which we used to update the firmware on our receiver and transmitter. Finally, we used DJI Assistant 2 to register and activate the DJI goggles and the DJI O4 module.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
316 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 216 0 R
/T (Betaflight:)
/E (Betaflight:)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
317 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1199 0 R
/E (We used Betaflight for flight controller software, specifically to set up rates and to ensure that the precision of the drone is increased \(e.g., reduced center sensitivity, increased expo for finer control when the drone is moving slowly, and we chose not to set a throttle limit since the drone is smaller compared to others, which means it has less lifting capacity\).)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
318 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1200 0 R
/E (It was also used for remapping the LED pad on the flight controller to output servo commands to the servo so that it can be controlled from the controller.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
319 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1201 0 R
/E (We used it for setting up the on-screen display \(OSD\), which provides the pilot with information about the battery voltage and an estimate of the flight time left before needing to land and switch out the battery.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
320 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1202 0 R
/E (PID tuning was performed to allow the drone to fly without jittering. This was done by adjusting the gyro filter multiplier to reduce the amount of vibrations detected by the gyro to ensure smoother flight.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
321 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1203 0 R
/E (Finally, we used it for reordering the motors to make sure that they spin the correct way using the built-in motor direction wizard in the Betaflight motor tab.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
322 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 216 0 R
/T (AM32 Configurator:)
/E (AM32 Configurator:)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
323 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1204 0 R
/E (We used the AM32.ca configurator as the ESC we selected to use on our drone utilized the AM32 firmware. Within the configurator, I set the motor KV setting to match the KV of the motor, as it reduces the amount of heat generated and improves efficiency.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
324 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1205 0 R
/E (Along with this, I also used the AM32 configurator to set a motor tune so that when the ESC starts up, it plays a song of my choice.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
325 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 217 0 R
/T (ExpressLRS Configurator:)
/E (ExpressLRS Configurator:)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
326 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1206 0 R
/E (Used to update the firmware on the Happy Model EP1 receiver on the drone, along with adding a binding phrase so that it cannot be connected to by unintended controllers.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
327 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1207 0 R
/E (Also used to update the ExpressLRS module in my RadioMaster Boxer controller so that the receiver and drone communicate smoothly.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
328 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 217 0 R
/T (DJI Assistant 2:)
/E (DJI Assistant 2:)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
329 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1208 0 R
/E (DJI Assistant 2 was used to set up and register both the DJI O4 PRO air unit and the DJI Goggles Integra.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
330 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1209 0 R
/E (Also used to update firmware and ensure that the power settings and channel selections follow the rules and regulations for the local area.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
331 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 217 0 R
/T (PID Tuning:)
/E (PID Tuning:)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
332 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 217 0 R
/E (PID tuning is a critical process in drone flight intended to ensure stability and responsiveness during operation. PID is an acronym for Proportional, Integral, and Derivative; it is a control loop feedback mechanism usually utilized by flight controllers. Each of these components plays a different role in how the drone reacts if it is off from some desired behavior:)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
333 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1210 0 R
/E (Proportional \(P\): The part responsible for the existing error develops a corrective force proportional to the size of the error. For a drone, this means the flight controller adjusts the motor speeds depending on how much the position or angle of the drone is away from the setpoint. However, a gain that is too high will cause oscillations when the system overcompensates.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
334 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1211 0 R
/E (Integral \(I\): This part deals with the integral error over time. When a drone drifts to one side for reasons such as unevenly distributed weight or wind, the integral term tries to balance it out by progressively incrementing power from the other direction until it eliminates the drifting. Too much use of this variable leads to instability and slow reaction.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
335 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1212 0 R
/E (Derivative \(D\): This term is responsive to the rate of change of the error and thus dampens the system to prevent overshoot and oscillation. It smooths movements so that the drone does not oscillate or jerk unnecessarily during stabilization.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
336 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 218 0 R
/T (PID Tuning Applied to Our Drone:)
/E (PID Tuning Applied to Our Drone:)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
337 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 218 0 R
/E (PID tuning is performed to optimize our drone for stable, smooth flight and with reliable and agile control for complex maneuvers. By using Betaflight, we adjust the PID value for pitch, roll and yaw based upon the results of flight testing.  This will allow us to ensure a reliable and agile drone for our complex maneuvers.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
